WEBVTT

00:00:04.171 --> 00:00:05.260
Hey, where are you going?

00:00:09.394 --> 00:00:11.004
That was close.

00:00:11.004 --> 00:00:13.355
Hermione, come out.
We've got loads to tell you.

00:00:13.355 --> 00:00:15.879
Go away.

00:00:15.879 --> 00:00:19.099
Wait till you see.
It's awful.

00:00:19.099 --> 00:00:21.754
[MYRTLE GIGGLES]

00:00:21.754 --> 00:00:23.539
Hermione?

00:00:23.539 --> 00:00:25.018
Are you okay?

00:00:27.499 --> 00:00:29.196
Do you remember
me telling you

00:00:29.196 --> 00:00:30.589
that the Polyjuice Potion

00:00:30.589 --> 00:00:32.287
was only for
human transformations?

00:00:32.287 --> 00:00:34.158
It was cat hair

00:00:34.158 --> 00:00:36.116
I plucked off
Millicent Bullstrode's robes.

00:00:39.119 --> 00:00:40.947
Look at my face.

00:00:40.947 --> 00:00:44.690
Look at your tail.

00:00:45.909 --> 00:00:48.477
[THUNDER CLAPS]

00:00:50.087 --> 00:00:51.741
RON: Have you spoken
to Hermione?

00:00:51.741 --> 00:00:54.396
She should be out of hospital
in a few days,

00:00:54.396 --> 00:00:57.312
when she stops
coughing up fur balls.

00:01:01.968 --> 00:01:03.970
What's this?

00:01:08.279 --> 00:01:09.933
RON: Yuck!

00:01:09.933 --> 00:01:13.328
Looks like Moaning Myrtle's
flooded the bathroom.

00:01:19.421 --> 00:01:21.814
[MYRTLE MOANING AND CRYING]

00:01:28.647 --> 00:01:31.955
Come to throw
something else at me?

00:01:31.955 --> 00:01:33.783
Why would I throw
something at you?

00:01:33.783 --> 00:01:36.220
Don't ask me.

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:38.744
Here I am,
minding my own business,

00:01:38.744 --> 00:01:42.095
and someone thinks it's funny
to throw a book at me.

00:01:42.095 --> 00:01:43.662
But it can't hurt

00:01:43.662 --> 00:01:45.795
if someone throws
something at you.

00:01:45.795 --> 00:01:47.666
I mean, it'll just
go right through you.

00:01:48.928 --> 00:01:50.277
Oh, sure!

00:01:50.277 --> 00:01:51.757
Let's all throw
books at Myrtle

00:01:51.757 --> 00:01:53.759
because she
can't feel it.

00:01:53.759 --> 00:01:56.153
Ten points if you get it
through her stomach!

00:01:56.153 --> 00:02:00.157
Fifty points if it goes
through her head!

00:02:00.157 --> 00:02:01.767
But who threw it
at you anyway?

00:02:01.767 --> 00:02:04.596
I don't know.
I didn't see them.

00:02:04.596 --> 00:02:06.772
I was just sitting
in the U-bend,

00:02:06.772 --> 00:02:09.601
thinking about death,

00:02:09.601 --> 00:02:11.908
and it fell through
the top of my head.

00:02:11.908 --> 00:02:13.605
Mm-hm.

00:02:14.911 --> 00:02:16.913
[SOBBING]

00:03:15.319 --> 00:03:17.887
My name...

00:03:17.887 --> 00:03:25.634
is Harry Potter.

00:03:38.037 --> 00:03:40.431
Do you know...

00:03:40.431 --> 00:03:44.827
anything about...

00:03:44.827 --> 00:03:50.920
the Chamber of Secrets?

00:04:00.973 --> 00:04:02.714
Can you...

00:04:02.714 --> 00:04:05.674
tell me?

00:05:08.388 --> 00:05:09.868
Excuse me.

00:05:09.868 --> 00:05:11.783
Could you tell me
what's going on here?

00:05:14.351 --> 00:05:16.309
Are you Tom Riddle?

00:05:18.094 --> 00:05:19.574
Hello.
Can you hear me?

00:05:39.855 --> 00:05:41.944
Riddle?

00:05:41.944 --> 00:05:43.423
Come.

00:05:43.423 --> 00:05:45.425
Professor Dumbledore.

00:05:47.863 --> 00:05:49.560
Dumbledore.

00:05:51.736 --> 00:05:53.346
It is not wise
to be wandering around

00:05:53.346 --> 00:05:55.740
this late hour, Tom.

00:05:55.740 --> 00:05:58.221
Yes, professor.
I suppose I--

00:05:58.221 --> 00:06:01.224
I had to see for myself
if the rumors were true.

00:06:01.224 --> 00:06:03.052
I'm afraid they are, Tom.

00:06:03.052 --> 00:06:04.531
They are true.

00:06:04.531 --> 00:06:06.272
About the school as well?

00:06:06.272 --> 00:06:08.013
I don't have a home to go to.

00:06:08.013 --> 00:06:10.755
They wouldn't really close
Hogwarts, would they, professor?

00:06:10.755 --> 00:06:13.453
I understand, Tom,
but I'm afraid...

00:06:13.453 --> 00:06:16.326
Headmaster Dippet
may have no choice.

00:06:16.326 --> 00:06:18.023
Sir, if it all stopped,

00:06:18.023 --> 00:06:22.201
if the person responsible
was caught...

00:06:23.812 --> 00:06:29.078
Is there something
you wish to tell me?

00:06:30.601 --> 00:06:32.821
No, sir. Nothing.

00:06:39.218 --> 00:06:40.872
Very well, then.

00:06:40.872 --> 00:06:43.092
Off you go.

00:06:43.092 --> 00:06:44.659
Good night, sir.

00:07:20.651 --> 00:07:22.174
Let's get you out of there--

00:07:22.174 --> 00:07:24.046
Evening, Hagrid.

00:07:24.046 --> 00:07:25.874
I'm going to have
to turn you in, Hagrid.

00:07:25.874 --> 00:07:28.833
I don't think you meant it
to kill anyone, but--

00:07:28.833 --> 00:07:30.922
You can't.
You don't understand.

00:07:30.922 --> 00:07:33.011
The dead girl's parents
will be here tomorrow.

00:07:33.011 --> 00:07:34.621
The least Hogwarts can do

00:07:34.621 --> 00:07:36.014
is make sure the thing
that killed their daughter

00:07:36.014 --> 00:07:37.276
is slaughtered.

00:07:37.276 --> 00:07:38.930
It wasn't him.

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:40.671
Aragog never killed no one.
Never.

00:07:40.671 --> 00:07:42.760
Monsters don't make good pets,
Hagrid.

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:44.196
Now stand aside.

00:07:44.196 --> 00:07:46.372
No!Stand aside, Hagrid!

00:07:46.372 --> 00:07:48.810
No!
Cistem Aperio!

00:07:56.252 --> 00:07:58.994
Arania Exumai.

00:07:58.994 --> 00:08:00.473
Aragog!

00:08:00.473 --> 00:08:01.910
Aragog!

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:03.868
I can't let you go.

00:08:03.868 --> 00:08:06.044
They'll have your wand
for this, Hagrid.

00:08:06.044 --> 00:08:07.611
You'll be expelled.

00:08:10.048 --> 00:08:13.617
Hagrid!

00:08:17.403 --> 00:08:19.971
Hagrid!

00:08:33.463 --> 00:08:35.378
Whoa.

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:43.603
It was Hagrid.

00:08:43.603 --> 00:08:46.737
Hagrid opened the Chamber
of Secrets 50 years ago.

00:08:46.737 --> 00:08:49.261
It can't be Hagrid.
It just can't be.

00:08:49.261 --> 00:08:51.176
We don't even know
this Tom Riddle.

00:08:51.176 --> 00:08:53.570
He sounds like a dirty,
rotten snitch to me.

00:08:53.570 --> 00:08:55.354
The monster had
killed somebody, Ron.

00:08:55.354 --> 00:08:57.313
What would any of us
have done?

00:08:57.313 --> 00:08:59.054
Look, Hagrid's our friend.

00:08:59.054 --> 00:09:01.578
Why don't we just go
and ask him about it?

00:09:01.578 --> 00:09:03.362
That would be a cheerful visit.

00:09:03.362 --> 00:09:05.277
"Hello, Hagrid.
Tell us...

00:09:05.277 --> 00:09:07.236
"have you been setting
anything mad and hairy

00:09:07.236 --> 00:09:08.715
loose in the castle lately?"

00:09:08.715 --> 00:09:10.326
Mad and hairy?

00:09:10.326 --> 00:09:11.806
You wouldn't be talking
about me, now, would you?

00:09:11.806 --> 00:09:14.156
No.
No.
No.

00:09:17.202 --> 00:09:19.291
What's that
you've got, Hagrid?

00:09:19.291 --> 00:09:22.904
Oh, it's Flesh-Eating
Slug Repellent.

00:09:22.904 --> 00:09:24.862
For the Mandrakes, you know?

00:09:24.862 --> 00:09:26.472
According to Professor Sprout,

00:09:26.472 --> 00:09:28.387
they've still got
a bit of growing up to do,

00:09:28.387 --> 00:09:29.911
but once their acne's
cleared up,

00:09:29.911 --> 00:09:32.609
we'll be able to chop them up
and stew them,

00:09:32.609 --> 00:09:35.177
and then we'll get those people
at the hospital un-Petrified.

00:09:36.569 --> 00:09:38.397
In the meantime, though,

00:09:38.397 --> 00:09:42.837
you three had best be looking
after yourselves. All right?

00:09:44.316 --> 00:09:45.970
Mmm.

00:09:50.757 --> 00:09:52.934
Hello, Neville.

00:09:52.934 --> 00:09:54.326
Harry...

00:09:54.326 --> 00:09:56.285
I don't know who did it,
but you'd better come.

00:09:56.285 --> 00:09:58.330
Come on!

